# snmpwalk — real-world examples

## Walk the system subtree (SNMP v1)

```sh
snmpwalk -Os -c public -v 1 switch01 system
```

## Walk the system subtree but skip the sysORTable

```sh
snmpwalk -Os -c public -v 1 -CE sysORTable switch01 system
```

## Poll interface counters on a homelab switch

```sh
snmpwalk -Os -c public -v 2c switch01 ifTable
```

## Use SNMPv3 with authentication and privacy

```sh
snmpwalk -v 3 -l authPriv -u david -a SHA -A "authpass" \
  -x AES -X "privpass" switch01 system
```

## Flag reference

| Flag        | What it does                                 |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| -v 1/2c/3   | SNMP protocol version                        |
| -c string   | community string (v1/v2c)                    |
| -Os         | print OIDs in short form                     |
| -CE oid     | end the walk before this OID                 |
| -l authPriv | v3 security level                            |

> On Tumbleweed the tools come from `sudo zypper install net-snmp`.
